  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: High pressure centered over the Desert \nSouthwest will keep temperatures well above normal today. Highs\nthis afternoon will reach upper 90s to low 100s, which will be\nnear-record to record heat for many locations. Heat Advisories \nare in effect this afternoon and evening across most of Northern \nand Central Nevada. Smoke from regional wildfires will reduce air\nquality across portions of Central and Northern Nevada. Smoke \nfrom the Ward Fire just south of Ely may impact Ely and the \nsurrounding towns as winds late this morning and afternoon \nincrease out of the south-southwest. \n\nTrough energy moving through the Pacific NW Sunday through Tuesday\nwill weaken the high pressure over the Great Basin slightly, which \nwill provide a few degrees of cooling relief to Northern and \nCentral NV. Temperatures will however remain above normal. High \npressure rebuilds over the region Wednesday through the remainder \nof next week, with afternoon highs climbing back up into the upper\n90s to low 100s. No convection or precipitation is expected in \nthe CWA for at least a week. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: \n\nHigh confidence in hot and dry weather continuing through the \nweekend and into the early part of next week. High forecast \nconfidence regarding a moderate risk of heat-related illnesses for\nheat-sensitive groups each afternoon through Sunday. High forecast \nconfidence in above normal temperatures persisting into at least \nthe middle of next week. Medium confidence in elevated to near- \ncritical fire weather conditions across northern Nevada during the\nafternoon periods Saturday through Monday with timing of strongest \nwind gusts coinciding with minimum RH values remaining more \nuncertain.",
